---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';

const checks = [
  {
    topic: 'Damage',
    text: 'Identify the broken mounting tab. Check whether the catalogue lists a bracket repair kit for that housing.',
  },
  {
    topic: 'Lamp version',
    text: 'Read the reference on the lamp and note which characters are unclear. Check it against the lighting equipment fitted to the vehicle.',
  },
  {
    topic: 'What comes in the box',
    text: 'Ask whether the bulb, control unit and mounting hardware are supplied with the housing or transferred from the original.',
  },
];
---

<Layout
  title="The headlamp still works. Its mounting tab is broken. | Parts Relay"
  description="Use a headlamp checklist to distinguish a failed bulb, a damaged bracket and a complete housing before requesting a replacement."
>
  <article class="team-page team-story">
    <div class="team-story-col team-story-head">
      <div class="team-story-tag">
        <img src="/assets/symbol.svg" alt="" /> At the counter
      </div>
      <h1 tabindex="-1">The headlamp still works. Its mounting tab is broken.</h1>
      <p class="team-story-dek">
        “Left headlamp” on a repair order could mean a bulb, a bracket or a complete assembly. When
        the lamp still lights but the housing moves, start with the mounting point.
      </p>
      <dl class="team-facts">
        <div>
          <dt>Assembly</dt>
          <dd>Left headlamp</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>Damage</dt>
          <dd>Broken mounting tab</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>Electrical check</dt>
          <dd>Bulb still lights</dd>
        </div>
      </dl>
      <figure class="team-story-photo">
        <img
          src="/assets/counter.webp"
          alt="An adviser points to the broken mounting tab on a headlamp while a parts specialist steadies the housing."
          width="768"
          height="432"
        />
        <button
          type="button"
          class="team-cover-open"
          data-team-open
          aria-expanded="false"
          aria-controls="team-counter-exchange"
        >
          <span aria-hidden="true">▶</span> Open the headlamp checklist
        </button>
        <div
          class="team-exchange"
          id="team-counter-exchange"
          role="region"
          aria-label="Headlamp checklist"
          data-checks={JSON.stringify(checks)}
          hidden
        >
          <button
            type="button"
            class="team-exchange-close"
            data-team-close
            aria-label="Close checklist"
          >
            ×
          </button>
          <div aria-live="polite" class="team-exchange-copy">
            <small></small>
            <blockquote></blockquote>
          </div>
          <div class="team-exchange-controls">
            <button type="button" data-team-prev aria-label="Previous check">
              ←
            </button>
            <span></span>
            <button type="button" data-team-next aria-label="Next check">
              →
            </button>
          </div>
        </div>
      </figure>
      <p class="team-lede">
        Call the distributor with two details from the bay. Describe what the lamp still does and
        where it has broken. Those details help the counter decide which parts drawing to open.
      </p>
      <div class="team-story-block">
        <h2>A loose housing</h2>
        <p>
          Record which fixing has failed. The parts catalogue may list a bracket repair kit for that
          version of the lamp. Check the repair procedure for the vehicle before deciding that the
          entire housing needs replacing.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="team-story-block">
        <h2>Which listing to open?</h2>
        <p>
          If the repair calls for the complete housing, say so on the enquiry. Ask the counter to
          identify the assembly for the left side and confirm which components the technician can
          transfer.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <section class="team-story-quote">
      <div>
        <blockquote>Which characters on the lamp label can the technician read?</blockquote>
        <p>Ask before quoting a replacement housing.</p>
      </div>
    </section>
    <div class="team-story-col team-story-after">
      <div class="team-story-block">
        <h2>Reading the label</h2>
        <p>
          A model may have several lighting packages. Read the manufacturer’s number directly from
          the lamp. Where the label is scuffed, leave a gap and tell the counter which end of the
          number is missing.
        </p>
        <p>
          The counter can use those characters to narrow the search. A complete label reading or the
          corresponding equipment detail is still needed to identify the replacement.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="team-story-block">
        <h2>The estimate stays open</h2>
        <p>
          Once the reference is clear, the distributor can say which housing it covers and what
          comes with it. Until then the adviser has a job to follow up, but no part number or
          delivery date to put on the estimate.
        </p>
      </div>
      <section class="team-record">
        <h3>Shift note for the headlamp job</h3>
        <dl>
          <div>
            <dt>Confirmed by the shop</dt>
            <dd>Complete left housing requested. Bulb checked and working.</dd>
          </div>
          <div>
            <dt>Still open</dt>
            <dd>
              Unreadable suffix on the original lamp. Check the lighting package and the contents of
              the replacement assembly.
            </dd>
          </div>
          <div>
            <dt>Next action</dt>
            <dd>
              Workshop to confirm the suffix or equipment fitted. Distributor to compare it with the
              catalogue.
            </dd>
          </div>
          <div>
            <dt>Before quoting</dt>
            <dd>
              Ask the supplier for its price and lead time once the counter has the right entry.
            </dd>
          </div>
        </dl>
      </section>
      <aside class="team-story-next">
        <div>
          <h2>Write the note for the next shift</h2>
          <p>
            The handoff workshop includes a worksheet for recording what the shop confirmed and who
            owes the next call.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="team-actions">
          <a class="team-btn" href="/workshops/handoff/">
            Open the handoff worksheet
          </a>
          <a class="team-btn team-secondary" href="/repair-shops/">
            Shop intake guide
          </a>
        </div>
      </aside>
    </div>
    <div class="team-story-float">
      <span>Have a part to identify?</span>
      <a class="team-btn" href="/tools/enquiry-builder/">
        Write an enquiry
      </a>
    </div>
    <section class="team-cta">
      <div class="team-frame">
        <h2 class="team-h2">Ask about a headlamp</h2>
        <p>
          Copy the original lamp number into your enquiry. If part of it is unreadable, mark where
          the lettering wears off.
        </p>
        <div class="team-actions">
          <a class="team-btn" href="/tools/enquiry-builder/">
            <img src="/assets/symbol.svg" alt="" />
            Prepare a headlamp enquiry
          </a>
          <a class="team-btn team-secondary" href="/tools/vin-check/">
            Check the vehicle identifier
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </article>
</Layout>

<script>
  import '../../scripts/counter.js';
</script>
